cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  functional-standard-atlas: an attenuation-corrected, territory-resolved
  benchmark of variant effect predictors against saturation genome editing
message: >-
  If you use this software or the derived data, please cite both the software
  (this file) and the accompanying paper listed under preferred-citation.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Zhang
    given-names: Ningyi
    affiliation: Department of Biological Sciences, National University of Singapore
    email: cliffzhang@u.nus.edu
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0004-3020-4044"
repository-code: "https://github.com/oneone00-11/functional-standard-atlas"
abstract: >-
  A frozen functional-standard atlas of 64,178 saturation genome editing
  variants across seven cancer susceptibility genes, with nineteen variant
  effect predictors scored under pinned pipelines, per-stratum measurement
  reliability estimates, and an attenuation-corrected territory map.
keywords:
  - variant effect prediction
  - saturation genome editing
  - multiplexed assays of variant effect
  - benchmarking
  - measurement reliability
  - attenuation correction
  - reproducibility
license: MIT
license-url: "https://opensource.org/licenses/MIT"
version: "2.4.2"
date-released: "2026-09-05"
identifiers:
  - type: doi
    value: "10.5281/zenodo.21828448"
    description: Concept DOI for all versions of the archived repository
references:
  - type: data
    title: MaveDB
    notes: >-
      Source saturation genome editing measurements. Deposits
      urn:mavedb:00000097-0-2 (BRCA1), 00001225-a-1 (BRCA2), 00001250-a-2
      (BARD1), 00001259-a-2 (PALB2), 00000662-0-1 (BAP1), 00000673-0-1
      (RAD51C), 00000675-a-1 (VHL). The frozen assay matrix is released CC BY
      4.0; the score matrices additionally carry nineteen predictor columns
      under mixed terms, eight of them more restrictive than CC BY 4.0 and
      three with no terms located. See LICENSE-DATA, and
      results/predictor_resources_v1.tsv for the per-column licences.
    authors:
      - name: MaveDB
    url: "https://www.mavedb.org"
preferred-citation:
  type: article
  title: "Measurement reliability bounds functional benchmarks and relocates where variant effect prediction fails"
  authors:
    - family-names: Zhang
      given-names: Ningyi
  year: 2026
  journal: "Submitted"
